2026-04-05 13:16:18.303 | 507086 (507086) | DEBUG    | Processing tool event with attributes: {'gen_ai.tool.name': 'open_files', 'gen_ai.tool.call.id': 'pyd_ai_ec401c4338464178b0ebbd08bbd2b202', 'tool_arguments': '{"file_paths":["tasks.txt"]}', 'logfire.msg': 'running tool: open_files', 'logfire.json_schema': '{"type": "object", "properties": {"tool_arguments": {"type": "object"}, "tool_response": {"type": "object"}, "gen_ai.tool.name": {}, "gen_ai.tool.call.id": {}}}', 'logfire.span_type': 'span', 'tool_response': '["Successfully opened tasks.txt:\\n\\n````text\\n   0 I\'ve completed my initial exploration of the Workspace Layout components and identified several key areas where robustness and\\n   1 visual standardization can be further improved. These components form the structural foundation of the AI Builder, making their\\n   2 stability and aesthetic consistency paramount for a professional \\"Intelligence Suite.\\"\\n   3 \\n   4                                                          Issues Identified\\n   5 \\n   6  1 BuilderLayout.tsx — Layout Stability:\\n   7     • The h-[calc(100vh-64px)] calculation is functional but lacks a robust fallback if the global Header height changes or fails\\n   8       to render.\\n   9     • Lacks explicit transition states for when sidebars are toggled, which could lead to layout \\"jumps.\\"\\n  10  2 BuilderCanvas.tsx — Viewport Integrity:\\n  11     • The zoomLevel transform lacks a requestAnimationFrame guard, which could lead to stuttering during rapid zoom interactions.\\n  12     • The \\"Vignette\\" shadow and ambient gradients are functional but don\'t strictly align with the \\"Neural Buffer\\" lighting\\n  13       established in other modules.\\n  14  3 BuilderSidebar.tsx — Ingestion & State resilience:\\n  15     • The w-[400px] width is hardcoded, which might not be optimal for smaller viewports or high-density technical analysis.\\n  16     • isCollapsed logic is based on !activeKey, but doesn\'t handle cases where the key might be stale or out-of-sync with the\\n  17       parent workspace.\\n  18  4 BuilderHeader.tsx — Project Identity:\\n  19     • (Requires expansion to verify), but likely needs hardening for projectName updates and \\"Active Sync\\" pulses.\\n  20 \\n  21                                                         Implementation Plan\\n  22 \\n  23  1 Harden BuilderLayout.tsx:\\n  24     • Implement CSS variables for layout dimensions (--workspace-h, --sidebar-w) to enable more flexible and robust scaling.\\n  25     • Add a motion.main container from Framer Motion to ensure smooth structural shifts when sidebars expand/collapse.\\n  26  2 Refactor BuilderCanvas.tsx:\\n  27     • Standardize the atmospheric grid (28px, 1.5px center) and ensure it\'s perfectly synchronized with the BuilderSidebar.\\n  28     • Implement a \\"Spectral Overlay\\" during high-latency RAG operations to signal the document is being \\"probed\\" by AI.\\n  29  3 Harden BuilderSidebar.tsx:\\n  30     • Add defensive checks for the panels object to prevent crashes on empty or malformed sidebar configurations.\\n  31     • Implement a \\"Stable Manifest\\" footer inside the sidebar container to match the project aesthetic.\\n  32  4 Standardize SidebarContainer.tsx & SidebarSection.tsx:\\n  33     • Ensure these sub-containers strictly follow the technical typography and 28px dot-grid standards.\\n  34 \\n  35                                                        Clarifying Questions\\n  36 \\n  37  • For the Builder Canvas, should I implement a \\"Safe Zone\\" indicator (crop marks) when in high-fidelity preview mode to mimic the\\n  38    physical A4 layout established in A4Page.tsx?\\n  39  • In the Builder Header, if a project rename fails, should I implement an optimistic rollback similar to the security settings\\n  40    pattern?\\n  41 \\n  42 \\n  43 \\n  44 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n  45 \\n  46                                                                                                                                      \\n  47 \\n  48                                                                                                                                      \\n  49  my Answers:                                                                                                                       \\n  50                                                                                                                                      \\n  51   1 Should I implement Framer Motion for sidebar transitions, or stick to CSS-only?                                                  \\n  52     Animated (Framer Motion)                                                                                                         \\n  53   2 Would you like to see physical \'Crop Marks\' on the document canvas in preview mode?                                              \\n  54     Add Crop Marks \\n````"]'}
