2026-04-05 14:38:40.146 | 640838 (640838) | DEBUG    | Model response text: I have successfully refactored the layout builder and its sub-components to achieve a flatter, more functional aesthetic by removing glassmorphism, highlights, and shadows. I also implemented global smooth scrolling.

### Changes Summary

#### 1. Global Styling (`src/app/globals.css`)
- Added `scroll-behavior: smooth;` to the `html` element to ensure consistent smooth scrolling across the entire application.

#### 2. Builder Header (`BuilderHeader.tsx`)
- Removed `backdrop-blur-3xl`, `bg-background/40`, and `shadow-2xl` from the main header.
- Simplified the Logo HUD by removing custom inset shadows and using a lighter background.
- Removed the shadow from the "Active Hub" status indicator.
- Refactored the action pill container to remove `backdrop-blur-md` and `shadow-inner`.
- Removed the `shadow-[0_0_24px_...]` and `ring-inset` from the "Save Project" button.
- Replaced the white "pulsing" shadow on the unsaved changes indicator with a standard `bg-primary` pulse.

#### 3. Sidebar Components (`BuilderSidebar.tsx` & `SidebarContainer.tsx`)
- Removed `backdrop-blur-3xl` and `bg-background/40` from the main sidebar.
- Removed `backdrop-blur-2xl` and `ring-inset` from the `SidebarContainer` header.
- Removed the ambient bottom fade from the sidebar content area.

#### 4. Builder Canvas (`BuilderCanvas.tsx`)
- Removed ambient gradients used for depth.
- Removed `backdrop-blur-3xl` and `shadow-2xl` from the "Neural Probing" processing HUD.
- Removed `backdrop-blur-xl` from the toolbar.
- Refactored the Zoom HUD to remove `backdrop-blur-3xl`, `shadow-[...]`, and `ring-inset`.
- Removed `backdrop-blur-md` from all zoom control tooltips.

#### 5. Interactive UI Components (`CollapsibleSidePanel.tsx` & `SidebarSection.tsx`)
- Removed custom shadows and `ring-2 ring-white/20` from active panel buttons.
- Removed the premium highlight overlay from active icons.
- Removed `backdrop-blur-xl` and `shadow-2xl` from panel tooltips.
- Removed `shadow-inner` from the vertical architectural line in sidebar sections.

The workspace now features a cleaner, high-density look focused on functional clarity rather than decorative effects.

Would you like me to perform any further refinements to the UI or focus on a different module?


